.TH decomp16 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
decomp16 \- uncompress a 16-bit .Z file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B decomp16
[\fB\-\fIn\fR] [\fIinput\fR [\fIoutput\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B decomp16
reads a file compressed by the old Unix
.B compress
and writes the original.  With no file names it reads standard input and
writes standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \- n
Split the work over
.I n
passes, 0 to 4, which trades time for memory.  On a machine this size
that trade is sometimes the difference between decompressing a file and
not.
.SH NOTES
Decompression only: there is no compressor here.  16-bit codes are the
limit, which is what
.B compress
produced by default.
.PP
.BR man (1)
will read a compressed manual page through this, if one is installed
with a
.B .Z
suffix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR tar (1)
